WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.900
Whether it's mountaineering, or marijuana. Trekking to Everest, or tripping on LSD.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.680
Getting as high as you can has always been central to the Nepal tourist experience.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.720
This is the story of an American president who tried to nip communism in the bud

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.700
by destroying a Himalayan hippie shangri-la.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.820
But in stopping the smokers he sparked a Maoist blowback.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.980
The hippie trail followed the footsteps
of the ancient Silk Road.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:37.980
But instead of trading textiles, its travelers swapped the post-war social conformity of the Western world

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.060
for dreams of enlightenment in the East.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.660
Some were fleeing the Vietnam War draft, while others came to find themselves.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:51.760
For whatever reason, every year from 1965 to 1973, tens of thousands of young people bussed or hitch-hiked

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.100
the overland route from Istanbul to Kathmandu.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:00.000
And the terminus of the hippie trail was a
single bustling urban lane, called Jhonche,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.200
rechristened by its new inhabitants as Freak Street.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:59.520
America's public enemy number one in the United States, is drug abuse.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.940
This will be a worldwide offensive, dealing with the problems of sources of supply

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.740
as well as Americans who may be stationed abroad wherever they are in the world.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:15.820
A number of young Americans have become addicts as they serve abroad.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.680
Whether in Vietnam or Europe, or other places.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:56.000
Whether or not these young men are tuned in, they've certainly dropped out of the society they knew.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.120
Together they've quietly rejected the practical Western world,

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.440
and seem not at all sure that they'll ever want to return.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:13.540
The hippies weren't the only ones
angered by prohibition.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:17.120
In western Nepal, far from the capital city of Kathmandu,

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.740
hashish cultivation was the primary source of income.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.600
Sellers and growers were arrested.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.100
Private property with marijuana growing on it was forfeited to the state.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:32.980
The destruction of the marijuana crops pushed tens of thousands of subsistence farmers

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.980
to the brink of starvation.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:48.440
Seeing political opportunity in economic
collapse, a communist party exploited local grievances,

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:54.340
and persuaded residents that only a violent overthrow of the government would solve their problems.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:04.880
Nixon's global war on drugs was fueling
the communist ideology he was trying to contain.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.160
And we will never surrender our
friends to communist aggression.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:19.880
By the "Just Say No" Reagan-era, drug prohibition had opened new opportunities for corruption

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.120
that led all the way to Nepal's royal family.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.620
King Birendra and I have each discovered a new friend.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:30.620
A blockbuster report by Nepalese journalist, Padam Thakurathi,

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.960
implicated the king's brothers in Nepal's booming heroin trade.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.940
The government immediately shut down Thakurathi's newspaper.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:44.600
Then, at 3 o'clock in the morning, a bodyguard of the royal family entered Thakurathi's home,

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.640
and aimed a gun 18 inches from his head.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.440
Shot in the face, Thakurathi survived the attack.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:56.800
He lost an eye, but lived to expose the royal family's involvement in black-market heroin.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.720
This is a quick escape from grim reality.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.060
Today, Nepal remains a thriving hub for heroin and hashish.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.260
With stories of drug busts, addiction, and violence,

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:14.400
mainstays of Nepal's television news coverage.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:22.900
By 2006 the Maoists controlled 80% of
the country.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:27.560
The insurgency based in Roma had grown into a national political force

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:33.060
that paralyzed the nation with a series of national strikes and armed resistance to the king.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:39.500
After a decade-long civil war that claimed 17,000 lives, Nepal's monarchy was abolished,

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.700
and the Communists elected to power.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:45.880
The Maoist have surged ahead past both the mainstream Left Party,

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.480
the UML, as well as the Nepali Congress.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:08:01.100
Today, Nepal's political situation has calmed down, and Freak Street is looking a little bit lonely.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:06.820
Katmandu's hippie past is running high
on nostalgia and low on foot traffic.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:11.100
The erstwhile hippie haven is now a hangout for hipsters.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:15.020
Artisanal coffee shops, outnumber head shops.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:19.780
And the old Eden hashish Centre is just an ordinary budget hotel.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.560
Despite a small political movement to legalize hashish,

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.400
marijuana is legal one day a year,

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.220
for religious purposes only.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:36.920
The rest of the time, tourists and locals take their chances on the black market.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:43.000
With its wild days behind it Freak Street has mostly dropped the drug trade,

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.020
and reinvented itself as a destination for mountain trekking.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.060
These days the real action is in Thamel.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.040
A short walk from Freak Street, Kathmandu's thumping nightlife hotspot

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.580
offers visitors every kind of indulgence that was available during Freak Street's heyday,

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:09.580
and many more that the hippies couldn't have imagined on their wildest trip.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:18.820
And a recent retro hit is reviving Kathmandu's hippy heritage.

